        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="y5xzyNHOv3AjmiNJnoz2-236" value="&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;0&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;" parent="MQ5YCEGSpXZeGLRsvfkm-73" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="125.71428571428572" y="255.98459477561954" width="23.57142857142857" height="16.79839249832552" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MQ5YCEGSpXZeGLRsvfkm-81" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;In 2nd level we must lookup into the Reservation Stations only if we have more reservation station ( we can do this without using a CAM because each instruction will access a RS entry with both operands at the same time. It won&#39;t ever happen that an instruction will access the same entry to put operand in different clock cycles), take a decision and create a fill request. At the same time we must compute the usage of the reservation station, and output it to the 1st level dispatcher.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Issuing the istruction operand to the reservation stations is not going to need an highly parallel approach since the #instruction issued are going to be equal to the superscalarity of our core (i.e. 4). A highly parallel and flexible interconnection is not needed.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-60" y="-190" width="470" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MQ5YCEGSpXZeGLRsvfkm-83" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;The total number of requests issued per cycle from the reservation station, of each lane, is equal to the number of processing element at our disposal per lane * the number of operands.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Same logic for the number of DS regs being swapped&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="810" y="-169.54000000000002" width="220" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MQ5YCEGSpXZeGLRsvfkm-86" value="" style="group" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="1">
